(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate an actionable 'Point-of-View' \(POV\) statement and derive three 'How Might We' \(HMW\) questions for an overworked intensive care nurse managing complex infusion pumps.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Formulation of the Point-of-View \(POV\) Statement:) Tj
T*
(   - Formula: [Specific User] needs [Actionable Need] because [Surprising Root Insight].) Tj
T*
(   - POV: 'A busy pediatric ICU nurse needs a rapid, fool-proof way to verify weight-based) Tj
T*
(   medication dosages on multiple infusion pumps during emergency resuscitations because the) Tj
T*
(   cognitive fatigue from converting milligrams to milliliters under flashing visual alarms makes) Tj
T*
(   her terrified of making a fatal dosing calculation error.') Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Derivation of Three Strategic 'How Might We' \(HMW\) Questions:) Tj
T*
(   - HMW 1 \(Amplify the Good / Automate Complexity\):) Tj
T*
(   'How might we automate weight-based dosage recalculations directly between the hospital) Tj
T*
(   electronic health record and the smart pump, eliminating manual mental arithmetic entirely?') Tj
T*
(   - HMW 2 \(Remove the Bad / Sensory Environment\):) Tj
T*
(   'How might we redesign the pump's acoustic and visual warning system so that non-critical) Tj
T*
(   alerts do not shatter the nurse's concentration during critical dosing setups?') Tj
T*
(   - HMW 3 \(Explore the Opposite / Collaborative Verification\):) Tj
T*
(   'How might we transform medication double-checking from a stressful administrative interruption) Tj
T*
(   into an effortless, 3-second tactile verification between two nurses?') Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
