(   1. Definitions and Operational Differences:) Tj
T*
(   - Prescriptive Step-by-Step Instruction:) Tj
T*
(   * Script: 'Click on the blue Settings icon. Select Network Configuration. Type 192.168.1.1 into) Tj
T*
(   the Gateway IP box. Click Save.') Tj
T*
(   * Flaw: Tests whether the user can read and follow instructions; reveals zero insights about) Tj
T*
(   interface discoverability or user mental models.) Tj
T*
(   - Goal-Directed Task Scenario:) Tj
T*
(   * Script: 'You have just moved into a new apartment and need to connect your laptop to your) Tj
T*
(   home wireless network. Use the application to configure your network connection so you can) Tj
T*
(   browse the internet.') Tj
T*
(   * Strength: Sets the overarching human objective and motivation, leaving the user completely) Tj
T*
(   free to explore, stumble, search, and navigate naturally.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Essential Characteristics of High-Impact Scenarios:) Tj
T*
(   - Realistic Context & Motivation: Grounded in a believable, authentic life situation.) Tj
T*
(   - Actionable Objective: Clear definition of what success looks like, without hinting at the) Tj
T*
(   specific UI path or button labels.) Tj
T*
(   - Non-Leading Terminology: Avoids using the exact words that appear on the interface buttons,) Tj
T*
(   preventing simple keyword matching by participants.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
