(   [Problem Statement]: Explain how 'Sensory and Physical Empathy' informs the hardware and software design of ruggedized industrial mobile computers used in sub-zero warehouse freezers.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Environmental & Human Physical Constraints:) Tj
T*
(   - Temperature: Commercial sub-zero warehouse freezers operate at -30?C \(-22?F\).) Tj
T*
(   - Sensory & Physical Degradation: Workers wear heavy insulated thermal gloves, eliminating fine) Tj
T*
(   motor finger dexterity; exhaled breath causes condensation and frost on displays; cold) Tj
T*
(   temperatures numb tactile nerve endings in fingertips.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Empathetic Hardware Engineering Solutions:) Tj
T*
(   - Resistive or Glove-Tuned Capacitive Touchscreens: Standard capacitive glass screens require) Tj
T*
(   bare skin conductivity; ruggedized units employ glove-optimized sensors with amplified) Tj
T*
(   capacitive sensitivity.) Tj
T*
(   - Large Physical Tactile Keys: Supplementing touchscreens with physical, widely spaced) Tj
T*
(   elastomeric keys with deep travel distances and audible tactile clicks, allowing positive) Tj
T*
(   confirmation through thick gloves.) Tj
T*
(   - Integrated Internal Screen Heaters: Installing optical heating elements behind the LCD to) Tj
T*
(   prevent liquid crystal freezing and vapor condensation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Software Interaction Adaptations:) Tj
T*
(   - High-contrast monochromatic color themes; massive touch targets \(minimum 48x48 mm\);) Tj
T*
(   voice-directed picking prompts via industrial headsets; eliminating multi-touch pinch-to-zoom) Tj
T*
(   gestures in favor of dedicated physical hardware scan triggers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
