(   2. Insights Uncovered Across a 12-Hour Oncology Shift:) Tj
T*
(   - Interruption Dynamics: An oncologist is interrupted by phone calls, pagers, and nursing) Tj
T*
(   questions on average once every 6 minutes. Each interruption causes software context loss; when) Tj
T*
(   returning to the EMR, the doctor must re-navigate multiple screens to resume patient charting.) Tj
T*
(   - Session Timeout Agony: Strict 5-minute security logout policies force the oncologist to) Tj
T*
(   re-type complex 16-character alphanumeric passwords over 70 times per shift, generating immense) Tj
T*
(   cognitive frustration.) Tj
T*
(   - Workarounds Under Pressure: To save time, doctors scribble patient chemotherapy doses on) Tj
T*
(   surgical glove cuffs, transcribing them hours later when quiet, introducing terrifying clinical) Tj
T*
(   error vulnerabilities.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Survey Blind Spots:) Tj
T*
(   - On a survey, the oncologist rates software security as 'acceptable' because they) Tj
T*
(   intellectually understand HIPAA regulations. Shadowing reveals that the implementation of) Tj
T*
(   security is actively endangering patient safety through cognitive exhaustion.) Tj
T*
